{"id": "af78bc00-c0f6-4bfc-8cf0-d411f49b54ee", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "There isn't actually a single fixed "default" CIDR block that AWS assigns automatically to a new VPC — when you create a VPC, you must specify the IPv4 CIDR block yourself (e.g., `10.0.0.0/16`). AWS doesn't pick one for you for custom VPCs.

That said, you might be thinking of the **default VPC** that AWS automatically creates in each region for new accounts — that one does use a fixed CIDR: `172.31.0.0/16`.

